Subject: [PATCH] Define gSharedMemoryKey inside the in-process API TU

Upstream defines `gSharedMemoryKey` in OpenGLExampleBrowser.cpp (the
desktop GUI entry point). We strip that file from the build because it
pulls in real GL — but SharedMemoryInProcessPhysicsC_API.cpp still does
`extern int gSharedMemoryKey;` and writes to it from a handful of
`b3CreateInProcessPhysicsServer*` paths that the Python binding reaches
through `pybullet.connect(...)`. Result: an undefined import lands in
the .so's export table and Pyodide's dynamic loader rejects it at
import time with `bad export type for 'gSharedMemoryKey': undefined`.

Promote the extern to a definition in the same TU that uses it. The
default `-1` matches what the upstream definition used.
---
 examples/SharedMemory/SharedMemoryInProcessPhysicsC_API.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/examples/SharedMemory/SharedMemoryInProcessPhysicsC_API.cpp b/examples/SharedMemory/SharedMemoryInProcessPhysicsC_API.cpp
--- a/examples/SharedMemory/SharedMemoryInProcessPhysicsC_API.cpp
+++ b/examples/SharedMemory/SharedMemoryInProcessPhysicsC_API.cpp
@@ -271,7 +271,7 @@
 	return (b3PhysicsClientHandle)cl;
 }

-extern int gSharedMemoryKey;
+int gSharedMemoryKey = -1;

 B3_SHARED_API b3PhysicsClientHandle b3CreateInProcessPhysicsServerFromExistingExampleBrowserAndConnect3(void* guiHelperPtr, int sharedMemoryKey)
 {
